From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ
Subject: [PATCH 0089] anv: report fd and host memory handle types only with their extensions

On top of the installed Mesa prod8 (bf8592b4 = src/mesa-prod8). Built in a copy (src/mesa-cts1, build-cts1, same
meson options as build-prod8); NOT installed (test package ~/b580/mesa-cts1-test).

vkGetPhysicalDeviceExternalBufferProperties and vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2 (with
VkPhysicalDeviceExternalImageFormatInfo) reported OPAQUE_FD and DMA_BUF as exportable and importable, and
HOST_ALLOCATION as importable, whether or not VK_KHR_external_memory_fd, VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf and
VK_EXT_external_memory_host are supported. On Linux they always are (xe; i915 with userptr), so nothing
changes there. With xemac (macOS) ANV_FD_SHARING is false: no fd extension is exposed, the device has no
vkGetMemoryFdKHR entry point (vkGetDeviceProcAddr returns NULL), yet the queries promised exportable dma-bufs:
- dEQP-VK.drm_format_modifiers.bound_to_dma_buf.* (checkSupport tests only VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier)
  found DMA_BUF exportable for every modifier, allocated exportable memory and called getMemoryFdKHR = NULL:
  SIGSEGV in deqp-vk (64 crashes).
- dEQP-VK.api.external.memory.{opaque_fd,dma_buf}.*.info: "Physical device claims to support handle type but
  required extensions are not supported" (6 fails).
A handle type whose extension is not supported is now reported as unsupported: compatibleHandleTypes =
handleType, no features (buffers); VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED (images), as for any other unsupported type.

Generated-by: LLM

